  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 291702\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n800 AM HST Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nActive Systems:\nThe National Hurricane Center is issuing advisories on Tropical\nStorm Vance, located about one hundred miles south-southeast of the\nsouthern tip of the Baja California Peninsula.\n\nWell Southeast of the Hawaiian Islands:\nA broad area of low pressure is likely to develop well to the\nsoutheast of the Hawaiian Islands this weekend or early next week.\nThereafter, environmental conditions appear generally favorable for\nsome slow development of this system as it moves westward to\nwest-northwestward into the Central Pacific basin.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...30 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Evans/Hagen\nNNNN",
